00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:38.880
So my other creepy movie theater story happened
10 years ago when I went to go see the movie

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:39.880
1408.

00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:40.880
I loved 1408.

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:43.570
I think it’s one of the most underrated
Stephen King movies.

00:00:43.570 --> 00:00:46.339
If you aren’t familiar with the film, it’s
based off of a short story about an author

00:00:46.339 --> 00:00:50.510
who writes about haunted places, and someone
challenges him to stay in this supposedly

00:00:50.510 --> 00:00:52.699
haunted hotel room in New York City.

00:00:52.699 --> 00:00:56.650
He tries to stay overnight in the room, but
soon finds himself unable to distinguish hallucinations

00:00:56.650 --> 00:00:59.140
from reality, and unable to escape room 1408.

00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:04.350
I went to go see this movie with my two friends…
let’s just call them Billy and Bobby.

00:01:04.350 --> 00:01:06.009
Because those were their actual names.

00:01:06.009 --> 00:01:10.439
As I mentioned, this movie came out in 2007,
so we were in 7th grade at the time.

00:01:10.439 --> 00:01:14.060
We had all just gotten to the age where we
were old enough to have our own cell phones,

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:18.440
so my parents would just drop me off at the
movies with my Sanyo PCS Vision Phone, and

00:01:18.440 --> 00:01:19.570
I could call to get picked up afterwards.

00:01:19.570 --> 00:01:25.340
That evening, we had gotten to the theater
a bit late, so we were just walking in right

00:01:25.340 --> 00:01:26.619
as the movie was starting.

00:01:26.619 --> 00:01:30.319
About 30 minutes in or something is the part
of the movie where the protagonist, uhh let’s

00:01:30.319 --> 00:01:34.390
just call him Mike Enslin, because that’s
his actual name, is getting settled in the

00:01:34.390 --> 00:01:36.200
hotel room when things start to go weird.

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:39.960
Now I know jump scares tend to get a lot of
hate these days, but I really like them when

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:44.350
they’re done right, and 1408 does an excellent
job of making the viewer put their guard down

00:01:44.350 --> 00:01:49.090
before a --

00:01:49.090 --> 00:01:52.900
So there are a bunch of jump scares in this
movie that involve the alarm clock, phone,

00:01:52.900 --> 00:01:54.789
and other appliances around the hotel room.

00:01:54.789 --> 00:01:58.159
Remember how I said that we walked into the
movie right as it was starting?

00:01:58.159 --> 00:02:02.999
Well, it turns out that we missed the silence
your phones reminder, and Billy had forgotten

00:02:02.999 --> 00:02:05.439
to turn his off before we sat down.

00:02:05.439 --> 00:02:09.741
So sure enough, at the exact moment of the
phone jump scare in the movie, Billy’s phone

00:02:09.741 --> 00:02:11.850
goes off at a startling volume.

00:02:11.850 --> 00:02:17.270
And I can’t even begin to describe the terror
of that moment.

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:19.620
The jump scare in the movie would have been
enough by itself.

00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:22.560
The volume of Billy’s phone ringing would
have been enough by itself.

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:27.650
But the fact that they happened at the exact
same time, made it feel for that one moment,

00:02:27.650 --> 00:02:30.640
like the haunts of the movie were in the seats
with us.

00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:33.740
This was also before the days where there
were a lot of ringtone options, so Billy had

00:02:33.740 --> 00:02:38.819
just had a generic analog phone ringtone that
almost matched the sound of the phone in 1408.

00:02:38.819 --> 00:02:42.280
It only took us a moment to figure out what
had happened, but that one moment was a moment

00:02:42.280 --> 00:02:47.180
of panic, and it was enough to put us on edge
for the rest of the 112 minute runtime.

00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:51.650
There’s not much else to this story, you
can look at it as a coincidence or you can

00:02:51.650 --> 00:02:54.409
look at it as something deeper, but one thing
you’re definitely going to want to look

00:02:54.409 --> 00:02:58.489
at is the next episode of True Fear, where
Cynder is going to be filling in, and filling

00:02:58.489 --> 00:03:01.519
you in on how a lunatic attacked her on the
bus.

